ry...This crest compares to a previous crest of 14.3\nfeet on 05/24/2004.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nEven 6 inches of fast-moving flood water can knock you off your feet\nand a depth of 2 feet will float your car. Never try to walk, swim,\nor drive through such swift water. If you come upon flood waters,\nstop, turn around and go another way.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/crp.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSCRP"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS84 KCRP 090113"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL SUNDAY AFTERNOON"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KCRP.FL.W.0026.000000T0000Z-260809T2035Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-09T15:35:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4012e8981516f4acc66aaf3deb0be40ca8d1a929.001.1,2026-08-07T20:14:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a4006eb38dda81396de878a3ee30877db05dc184.001.1,2026-08-07T08:43:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.422f915b9c8698a61ceeecbb773519636c1559f0.001.1,2026-08-06T20:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6c086fb0cb122a2dcaad2d633e16163ca1e2f740.002.1,2026-08-06T08:31:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cd351168adba7b138d4b2fd5b257e34ba80d69c4.002.1,2026-08-05T19:53:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.15a54361c4ea7596611f53154fbe235d68afe15a.002.1,2026-08-05T10:56:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cfe0cb53516243e5682c1b93f097af5f347ba9d1.002.1,2026-08-04T20:07:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0d85f3f3b48cc9017f55a16e1f1acf4cc74e9f0b.002.1,2026-08-